      "heading": "B — Audience, level and prerequisites: required vehicle equipment, lights, tires and glass",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience, level and prerequisites: required vehicle equipment, lights, tires and glass\nAudience: first-time Minnesota Class D applicants and the parents or owners who supply the vehicle for practice and for the road test.\nWhy it matters to a first-timer: equipment rules such as the two brake systems [A01], the headlight distances [A02] and the tread and tint limits [A03] are short numeric items on the written test, and the road test vehicle must meet them.\nLevel: straightforward recall with a few look-alike numbers (two headlight distances, two tint percentages); low to moderate load.\nPrerequisites: the road test vehicle requirements in chapter one.\n",
